    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.\n2. Determine the supplement of the complement.\n3. Find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.**\n\nThe complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 90 degrees. So, we need to find the angle \\( x \\) such that:\n\\[ 42^\\circ + x = 90^\\circ \\]\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = 90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ \\]\nSo, the complement of the 42-degree angle is \\( 48^\\circ \\).\n\n**Step 2: Determine the supplement of the complement.**\n\nThe supplement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 180 degrees. So, we need to find the angle \\( y \\) such that:\n\\[ 48^\\circ + y = 180^\\circ \\]\nSolving for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ \\]\nSo, the supplement of the complement is \\( 132^\\circ \\).\n\n**Step 3: Find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement.**\n\nThe supplement of the complement is already calculated in Step 2. Therefore, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is:\n\\[ \\boxed{132} \\]",
