    {
      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.\n2. Determine the supplement of the complement obtained in step 1.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle\nThe complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 90 degrees. Therefore, we need to find the angle \\( x \\) such that:\n\\[\n42^\\circ + x = 90^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = 90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ\n\\]\nSo, the complement of the 42-degree angle is \\( 48^\\circ \\).\n\n### Step 2: Determine the supplement of the complement\nThe supplement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 180 degrees. Therefore, we need to find the angle \\( y \\) such that:\n\\[\n48^\\circ + y = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny = 180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ\n\\]\nSo, the supplement of the 48-degree angle is \\( 132^\\circ \\).\n\nThus, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\(\\boxed{132}\\).",
